<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdul Rashid Dostum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdul Rashid Dostum is an Afghan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> militia leader and politician from the north of the country. He commanded a militia for the communist government, then switched sides in 1992, helping to bring down President Najibullah, and fought in the civil wars from his base at Mazar-i-Sharif. He was later a leader of the Northern Alliance against the Taliban and was vice-president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> from 2014 to 2020.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdul-rashid-dostum.jpg" alt="Abdul Rashid Dostum" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. State Department · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdul_Rashid_Dostum_in_September_2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
